# No production deploys (unlock: deskwave)

**Default for every agent session.** Production Neon, Cloudflare Pages prod, and Hetzner API prod stay untouched until the team is ready.

## Unlock word

**`deskwave`** — the user must type this exact word in the **same message** that asks you to run or recommend a blocked production operation.

Without **`deskwave`**:

- **Do not run** blocked commands.
- **Do not recommend** blocked commands as the next step.
- **Do not** offer prod deploy as an optional follow-up unless the user already unlocked.

When the user **has** said **`deskwave`**:

- Run **only** the specific prod operation they asked for.
- Include **`deskwave`** in the shell command string so hooks allow it (e.g. `DESKWAVE=deskwave pnpm run deploy:api:prod`).
- Remind them of `docs/architecture/deployment.md` (backup, diff, checklist) before executing.

## Blocked without unlock

| Pattern | Examples |
| ------- | -------- |
| Prod deploy scripts | `pnpm run deploy:api:prod`, `deploy:web:prod`, `migrate:prod`, `rollback:db:prod` |
| Remote Alembic | `alembic upgrade` against Neon `DATABASE_URL`, any `--db-url` pointing at hosted Postgres |
| Remote SQL | Mutating SQL against prod pooler/hosted URIs |

## Allowed without unlock

| Safe | Examples |
| ---- | -------- |
| Local stack | `pnpm run dev:docker`, `dev`, `db:migrate`, `db:reset:local` |
| Dev deploy | `deploy:api:dev`, `deploy:web:dev`, `migrate:dev`, `rollback:db:dev` |
| Backups / status | `backup:db:dev` / `:prod` (read dump), `env:status` |
| Local migrations in repo | Add **new** files under `apps/api/migrations/versions/` (never edit shipped ones) |

Shell hooks: `.cursor/hooks/guard-shell.sh`, `scripts/dev/prod-deploy-guard-lib.sh`.
